### Usability Improvement: Handle Expired Refresh Tokens on Logout

If a user attempts to log out with an expired refresh token, `verifyToken` will throw a `TokenExpiredError`, and the API will return a `401 AUTH_INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN` error. This can break client-side logout flows or show unnecessary error messages to the user.

Since an expired refresh token means the session is already invalid/inactive, we should treat this as a successful logout and return a `200 AUTH_LOGOUT_SUCCESS` response. This ensures a robust and seamless logout experience.

```javascript
    let decoded;
    try {
      decoded = verifyToken(refreshToken);
    } catch (error) {
      if (error.name === 'TokenExpiredError') {
        return sendSuccess(req, res, 200, 'AUTH_LOGOUT_SUCCESS', '已退出登录');
      }
      if (error.name === 'JsonWebTokenError') {
        return sendError(req, res, 401, 'AUTH_INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN', 'Invalid refresh token', '无效的刷新令牌');
      }
      throw error;
    }
```

